From b0318a1079fd5372e92290f3409ed18da564eb5d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: phlink <phlink@local>
Date: Wed, 29 Apr 2026 23:47:19 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] phlink: phase 10.01b: TufClient C++ skeleton + dev root +
 tests

In-tree pure-C++ TUF v1.0.32 metadata client backed by base::JSONReader,
a hand-rolled canonical-JSON encoder, crypto::sign::Verify(ED25519), and
boringssl SHA-256. No Rust crate, no hyper, no ring -- avoids violating
the Phase 9 boringssl-only crypto policy and stays off the network on
the verification path.

  * canonical_json.[h|cc] -- TUF-flavour canonical JSON (sorted keys,
    no whitespace, integers only).
  * metadata_client.[h|cc] -- TufClient::CreateWithRoot, IngestTimestamp,
    IngestSnapshot, IngestTargets, LookupTarget. Threshold signature
    verification (Ed25519), spec_version pinning (1.0.x), expires +
    rollback + version-pin enforcement, length+sha256 pinning across
    timestamp -> snapshot -> targets.
  * keys/dev_root.json -- 1-of-1 single-key dev root, ships only when
    phlink_updater_dev_root=true (default for now). Production root
    swaps in via plan 10-08.
  * metadata_client_unittest.cc -- 4 tests: AcceptsValidMetadata,
    RejectsExpiredTimestamp, RejectsRollback, RejectsBadSignature.
  * phlink_updater.gni, BUILD.gn -- source_sets + test() target +
    copy() to root_out_dir/phlink/keys/. Wired into //:chrome_test_targets.

See docs/dev/update-protocol.md (patch 0124) for the protocol spec
this implements.

Refs phase 10 plan 10-01b.
